      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ✅ **LGTM** — All checks pass. [[trajectory](go/traj/e6cceb68-2be5-4d16-8ef0-e5e2256a45af)]\n\n### Review Summary\n**Functionality \u0026 Security:**\n- The changes successfully resolve the heap buffer overflow vulnerabilities identified in earlier patchsets. The use of `__builtin_add_overflow` correctly prevents integer wrap-around when calculating the total allocation size (payload + header).\n- `plat_calloc` is cleanly simplified to use `sys_alloc` directly, eliminating redundant overflow checking and ensuring consistent error handling (triggering `k_oops()` instead of silently failing).\n- `plat_realloc` memory copy boundaries are safely bounded by the source block size via `sys_alloc_usable_size()`, preventing buffer over-reads when shrinking memory.\n- The use of `sys_alloc_usable_size()` to retrieve the accurate, requested size rather than the heap block size is robust and safe.\n\n**Style \u0026 Consistency:**\n- Using `ROUND_UP` from Zephyr cleanly replaces manual alignment macros.\n- The allocator interfaces are now unified and consistent.\n\n**Testing:**\n- The newly added `ztest` cases are excellent. Using `ztest_set_fault_valid(true)` to ensure that panics (like OOM or integer overflows) actually trigger the expected `k_oops()` is exactly the right way to test fatal error handling.\n- Core memory operations (resizing, growing, calloc zero-initialization) are heavily verified, protecting against future regressions.\n\nTAG\u003dagy\nCONV\u003d2f703dfc-9c08-4784-87ec-c4c3aa91cc34",
